STIG in Splunk (stigs_in_splunk)
================================

This software is an independent, Splunk-native implementation of STIG checklist
and review workflows. It is developed by Stephen Quinlan (learnda1ly) and is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or an official product of the U.S. Department
of Defense, DISA, NUWCDIVNPT, NAVSEA Warfare Centers, or the STIG Manager
project.

STIG Manager (behavioral and UX reference only)
-----------------------------------------------

[STIG Manager](https://github.com/NUWCDIVNPT/stig-manager) by NUWCDIVNPT /
NAVSEA Warfare Centers informed the *behavior and user experience* this project
aims to support. **This repository is not a fork of STIG Manager** and does not
include STIG Manager server, Node/Express, or ExtJS client source code.

STIG Manager’s own licensing is dual: MIT for non-client components and
GPL-3.0 for the ExtJS client. **This project does not ship the STIG Manager
ExtJS client or other GPL-3.0 client code.**

Documentation in this repo (for example `docs/FEATURE_PARITY.md` and
`docs/watcher-hec.md`) may reference STIG Manager APIs and concepts for
parity planning only.

STIGMan Watcher (schema reference only)
---------------------------------------

[STIGMan Watcher](https://github.com/NUWCDIVNPT/stigman-watcher) event and
ingest field shapes are used as a **compatibility reference** for HEC and
checklist ingest (for example `source_product` values and review JSON fields).
**Watcher source code is not copied into this repository.**

Third-party software
--------------------

Dependencies retain their own licenses, including but not limited to:

- Splunk Universal Configuration Console (UCC) tooling and generated app
  scaffolding
- SplunkUI / React and npm packages (see `ui/package-lock.json`)
- Vendored Python libraries under `lib/` when present (for example Splunk SDK
  for Python), each with its own license file

DISA STIG content
-----------------

This repository does **not** distribute DISA STIG XML libraries or official
STIG benchmark packages. Users must obtain STIG content from DISA under DISA’s
terms. Small synthetic or truncated fixtures under `tests/fixtures/` exist only
for automated tests and are not a STIG library distribution.

